From e7aa9d2f63c1932a7a0e6647e2d5cc591a6230e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:11:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Excluded devices: full bypass by IP, subnet or MAC (#88)

Requires: 020-sing-box-114-dns-http-client

Add "Excluded devices": full Forkop bypass by IP, subnet or MAC (#88)

New settings list routing_excluded_ips. For each listed device:

- nft: its traffic leaves the mangle chain before any section rule, so
  the exclusion no longer depends on section order (a bypass section
  with "Forced device routing" only works when it is placed first);
- DNS: its port-53 traffic is redirected to a new excluded-dns-in
  inbound (:1605) and answered like a source-aware bypass client:
  local resolver unless it returns a nested FakeIP, otherwise the
  upstream DNS. Without this the device would receive FakeIP answers it
  cannot reach once nft stops sending its traffic to sing-box. On
  sing-box >= 1.14 the evaluate/respond form is used;
- sing-box: a route rule sends IP entries to bypass-out before section
  rules, as a safety net.

Entries may be IPv4/IPv6 addresses, CIDRs or MAC addresses. A MAC keeps
matching after a new DHCP lease or an IPv6 privacy address change;
Gavr1024/forkop-mod resolves DHCP host names to IPs once at start, which
goes stale. Invalid entries are rejected by the validator and skipped by
nft. The LuCI field reuses the local-device picker and also offers MAC
addresses from host hints and DHCP leases.

Verified: tests/excluded_devices.sh (nft commands and order, generated
config for 1.13/1.14, validator); `sing-box check` and a short
`sing-box run` with the official 1.13.21 and 1.14.2 binaries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HEQfjBzS7Wos7AvTk18TDQ
